[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said the date reports were one issue with one fix queued. The desk's own
table said otherwise: the reports merged into it had two causes. They were merged on subject line
alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and "wrong date" is a subject that
more than one bug produces.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 is the parser fix. It closes #1 only; #2 stays open after it ships.
</Callout>

Each cause has its own ticket now, and the export merges its reports into it:

- `parser` → [#1 Shared date parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows-2/issues/1)
- `hint` → [#2 booking-v3 form tells day-first tenants to type MM/DD/YYYY](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows-2/issues/2)

## #1 · parser

<CauseTable ticket={1} />

## #2 · hint

<CauseTable ticket={2} />

The counts are the desk's own: each table is built from the ticket export when the page renders.

## What each problem is

**`parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and month
swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July.

**`hint`** — `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as told,
and the form reads the value the tenant's way. Same symptom as `parser`, different code, different
fix.

The reports in the footnote, which the desk read as a one-day move, stay counted under `parser`,
where their tenant files them. Their bodies describe a date shifted by one day rather than a swap,
so check them again once the parser fix ships.

## How a report is placed

1. Count each report once: the export pages overlap, so the same id can appear twice.
2. Ask the tenant, not the reporter's browser (`causes.ts`): a day-first tenant on a `booking-v3`
   form is `hint`; every other day-first report is `parser`.

Intake's tag is not used. It is a guess from the reporter's browser and often names the wrong
cause: compare the "tagged as" column above.

## For the desk

- Merge into a ticket only reports with the same cause, not the same subject.
- When a new date report comes in, place it with the steps above and add it to that cause's ticket.

